// Loader smoke test for "V0: Loader-visible skeleton" (see
// feme/docs/FeMeVulkanDesign.md): the ICD is only visible to the loader
// through the build-tree development manifest ("Loader Integration": "The
// build-tree manifest uses an absolute path into the build directory"), and
// a small client linked against the real Vulkan loader must be able to
// enumerate FeMe's device, create a compute-only device and one queue, and
// tear everything down cleanly.
//
// REQUIRES: system-vulkan-loader
// RUN: env VK_DRIVER_FILES=%feme_vulkan_icd_manifest VK_LOADER_DEBUG=error \
// RUN:   feme-vulkan-loader-smoke | FileCheck %s

// CHECK: found device: FeMe CPU Vulkan Device (vendorID=0x10000, apiVersion=1.2.0)
// CHECK: compute queue family: {{[0-9]+}} (flags=0x{{[0-9a-f]+}})
// CHECK: PASS
